content.text:
Now update updateHUD to render new rows with gap. Also record history call. Let's edit updateHUD.

Current block:
```
race.leaderTimer -= dt;
if (race.leaderTimer <= 0) {
  race.leaderTimer = 0.28;
  const leader = standings[0];
  dom.leaderboard.innerHTML = standings.map((row, i) => {
    const diff = (leader.progress - row.progress) * race.track.length;
    const gap = i === 0 ? 'LEAD' : (diff < 1 ? '0.0' : `+${(diff / 42).toFixed(1)}`);
    ...
  }).join('');
}
```

New:
```
race.leaderTimer -= dt;
if (race.leaderTimer <= 0) {
  race.leaderTimer = 0.24;
  const leader = standings[0];
  race.gapShown = race.gapShown || {};
  dom.leaderboardRows.innerHTML = standings.map((row, i) => {
    let gapSec;
    if (i === 0) gapSec = 0;
    else if (row.finished && leader.finished && leader.finishTime != null && row.finishTime != null) gapSec = Math.max(0,(row.finishTime - leader.finishTime)/1000);
    else gapSec = gapToLeaderSeconds(leader, row.progress, (row.speed + leader.speed) * 0.5);
    const prev = race.gapShown[row.name];
    const shown = prev == null ? gapSec : prev + (gapSec - prev) * 0.55;
    race.gapShown[row.name] = shown;
    const gap = i === 0 ? 'LEADER' : `+${shown.toFixed(3)}`;
    const leaderClass = i === 0 ? ' is-leader' : '';
    return `<div class="lb-row${row.isPlayer ? ' is-player' : ''}${leaderClass}">
      <span class="lb-pos">${i + 1}</span>
      <i class="lb-col" style="background:${row.color}"></i>
      <span class="lb-name">${row.name}</span>
      <span class="lb-gap">${gap}</span>
    </div>`;
  }).join('');
}
```
Note: gapToLeaderSeconds for i===0 not used. But smoothing of leader 0. For a car in P2 that becomes leader, gapShown target 0, smoothed to 0 over frames; displays "+0.xxx" while smoothing? i===0 shows 'LEADER' regardless. When it drops back to P2, its smoothed value may still be near 0 → "+0.001" briefly, acceptable. But gaps are relative to leader; when leader changes, all gaps jump. Smoothing handles.

However there's an issue: `gapToLeaderSeconds(leader,...)` where leader is the leader row; if row is P2 but leader has `history` empty at countdown, returns 0. During countdown all +0.000. Fine.

Record history in updateRace racing state. Add after updatePlayerProgress.

